    {
      "id": "scene-02",
      "title": "The Z-Basis: |0\u27e9 and |1\u27e9",
      "durationSeconds": 25,
      "startFrame": 601,
      "endFrame": 1350,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "By international convention, the standard computational basis corresponds to measurement along the Z-axis of the Bloch sphere. We denote these standard eigenstates as ket zero and ket one.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "The computational basis aligns with the Z-axis of measurement.",
          "startFrame": 601,
          "endFrame": 960
        },
        {
          "text": "Eigenstates are denoted |0\u27e9 and |1\u27e9.",
          "startFrame": 961,
          "endFrame": 1350
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_basis",
          "text": "Standard Z-Basis: B = { |0\u27e9, |1\u27e9 }",
          "role": "header",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            2.0,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_zaxis",
          "text": "\u03c3_z |0\u27e9 = +1|0\u27e9,   \u03c3_z |1\u27e9 = -1|1\u27e9",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_2_bg",
          "type": "background_plate",
          "source": "assets/backgrounds/deep_space_grid.png",
          "layer": "background"
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_2_stage",
          "type": "vector_diagram",
          "source": "procedural_blender_object",
          "layer": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "animationActions": [
        {
          "target": "vis_2_stage",
          "action": "fade_in_and_settle",
          "startFrame": 601,
          "durationFrames": 30
        }
      ],
      "assetsRequired": [
        "deep_space_grid.png",
        "ibm_quantum_palette.blend"
      ],
      "educationalPurpose": "Formalize the Z-basis eigenstates and Pauli-Z eigenvalues.",
      "transitionOut": "smooth_crossfade"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-03",
      "title": "Bra Vectors and Dual Space",
      "durationSeconds": 30,
      "startFrame": 1351,
      "endFrame": 2250,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "For every ket vector |\u03c8\u27e9 in our Hilbert space, there is a corresponding dual vector called a bra, written \u27e8\u03c8|. Mathematically, the bra is formed by taking the complex conjugate transpose of the column ket.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "For every ket |\u03c8\u27e9, the dual bra vector is \u27e8\u03c8| = (|\u03c8\u27e9)\u2020.",
          "startFrame": 1351,
          "endFrame": 1770
        },
        {
          "text": "The bra vector is the conjugate transpose row vector.",
          "startFrame": 1771,
          "endFrame": 2250
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_bra0",
          "text": "\u27e80| = [ 1, 0 ]",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            1.2,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_bra1",
          "text": "\u27e81| = [ 0, 1 ]",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            -0.4,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_3_bg",
          "type": "background_plate",
          "source": "assets/backgrounds/deep_space_grid.png",
          "layer": "background"
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_3_stage",
          "type": "vector_diagram",
          "source": "procedural_blender_object",
          "layer": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "animationActions": [
        {
          "target": "vis_3_stage",
          "action": "fade_in_and_settle",
          "startFrame": 1351,
          "durationFrames": 30
        }
      ],
      "assetsRequired": [
        "deep_space_grid.png",
        "ibm_quantum_palette.blend"
      ],
      "educationalPurpose": "Introduce bra vectors and conjugate transpose operations.",
      "transitionOut": "smooth_crossfade"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-04",
      "title": "The Inner Product & Orthonormality",
      "durationSeconds": 35,
      "startFrame": 2251,
      "endFrame": 3300,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "When a bra and ket meet, they form a bracket\u2014an inner product representing geometric overlap. The computational basis states are orthonormal: \u27e80|0\u27e9 equals one, \u27e81|1\u27e9 equals one, but \u27e80|1\u27e9 equals zero.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "A bra and ket form an inner product: \u27e8\u03c6|\u03c8\u27e9.",
          "startFrame": 2251,
          "endFrame": 2700
        },
        {
          "text": "Orthonormality: \u27e80|0\u27e9 = 1, \u27e81|1\u27e9 = 1, and \u27e80|1\u27e9 = 0.",
          "startFrame": 2701,
          "endFrame": 3300
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_ortho",
          "text": "\u27e8i|j\u27e9 = \u03b4_ij (Kronecker Delta)",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            1.0,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_overlap",
          "text": "\u27e80|0\u27e9 = 1 (Identical) | \u27e80|1\u27e9 = 0 (Orthogonal)",
          "role": "subheader",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            -0.8,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_4_bg",
          "type": "background_plate",
          "source": "assets/backgrounds/deep_space_grid.png",
          "layer": "background"
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_4_stage",
          "type": "vector_diagram",
          "source": "procedural_blender_object",
          "layer": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "animationActions": [
        {
          "target": "vis_4_stage",
          "action": "fade_in_and_settle",
          "startFrame": 2251,
          "durationFrames": 30
        }
      ],
      "assetsRequired": [
        "deep_space_grid.png",
        "ibm_quantum_palette.blend"
      ],
      "educationalPurpose": "Demonstrate the mathematical definition and geometric meaning of orthogonality.",
      "transitionOut": "smooth_crossfade"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-05",
      "title": "Decomposition of Arbitrary States",
      "durationSeconds": 30,
      "startFrame": 3301,
      "endFrame": 4200,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "Because {|0\u27e9, |1\u27e9} spans the entire two-dimensional space, we can project any state vector onto our basis using inner products. The amplitude \u03b1 is simply \u27e80|\u03c8\u27e9, and \u03b2 is \u27e81|\u03c8\u27e9.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "Any state decomposes as: |\u03c8\u27e9 = \u27e80|\u03c8\u27e9|0\u27e9 + \u27e81|\u03c8\u27e9|1\u27e9.",
          "startFrame": 3301,
          "endFrame": 3720
        },
        {
          "text": "Amplitudes \u03b1 = \u27e80|\u03c8\u27e9 and \u03b2 = \u27e81|\u03c8\u27e9 measure projection onto each basis axis.",
          "startFrame": 3721,
          "endFrame": 4200
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_decomp",
          "text": "\u03b1 = \u27e80|\u03c8\u27e9,   \u03b2 = \u27e81|\u03c8\u27e9",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            0.8,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_proj",
          "text": "|\u03c8\u27e9 = |0\u27e9\u27e80|\u03c8\u27e9 + |1\u27e9\u27e81|\u03c8\u27e9",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            -0.6,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_5_bg",
          "type": "background_plate",
          "source": "assets/backgrounds/deep_space_grid.png",
          "layer": "background"
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_5_stage",
          "type": "vector_diagram",
          "source": "procedural_blender_object",
          "layer": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "animationActions": [
        {
          "target": "vis_5_stage",
          "action": "fade_in_and_settle",
          "startFrame": 3301,
          "durationFrames": 30
        }
      ],
      "assetsRequired": [
        "deep_space_grid.png",
        "ibm_quantum_palette.blend"
      ],
      "educationalPurpose": "Show how projection onto basis vectors extracts probability amplitudes.",
      "transitionOut": "smooth_crossfade"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-06",
      "title": "The Completeness Identity",
      "durationSeconds": 25,
      "startFrame": 4201,
      "endFrame": 4950,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "By summing the outer products of our orthonormal basis, we obtain the identity operator: |0\u27e9\u27e80| + |1\u27e9\u27e81| equals the identity matrix I. This completeness relation ensures quantum operations preserve total geometry.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "Outer product sum: |0\u27e9\u27e80| + |1\u27e9\u27e81| = I.",
          "startFrame": 4201,
          "endFrame": 4560
        },
        {
          "text": "Completeness guarantees that probability is conserved across the space.",
          "startFrame": 4561,
          "endFrame": 4950
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_id",
          "text": "|0\u27e9\u27e80| + |1\u27e9\u27e81| = I = [ [1, 0], [0, 1] ]",
          "role": "formula",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            0.5,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_6_bg",
          "type": "background_plate",
          "source": "assets/backgrounds/deep_space_grid.png",
          "layer": "background"
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_6_stage",
          "type": "vector_diagram",
          "source": "procedural_blender_object",
          "layer": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "animationActions": [
        {
          "target": "vis_6_stage",
          "action": "fade_in_and_settle",
          "startFrame": 4201,
          "durationFrames": 30
        }
      ],
      "assetsRequired": [
        "deep_space_grid.png",
        "ibm_quantum_palette.blend"
      ],
      "educationalPurpose": "Introduce projection operators and the completeness relation.",
      "transitionOut": "smooth_crossfade"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-07",
      "title": "Physical Readout in the Z-Basis",
      "durationSeconds": 35,
      "startFrame": 4951,
      "endFrame": 6000,
      "narration": {
        "speaker": "QUALUTION Narrator",
        "text": "In physical quantum hardware\u2014whether transmon microwave resonators or ion-trap lasers\u2014readout devices measure qubits directly in this computational Z-basis, collapsing quantum superposition into classical bits.",
        "tone": "Authoritative, pedagogically clear, engaging",
        "pacingWpm": 130
      },
      "captions": [
        {
          "text": "Quantum hardware measurement devices operate in the Z-basis.",
          "startFrame": 4951,
          "endFrame": 5430
        },
        {
          "text": "Measurement projects the qubit onto either |0\u27e9 or |1\u27e9.",
          "startFrame": 5431,
          "endFrame": 6000
        }
      ],
      "onScreenText": [
        {
          "id": "txt_meas",
          "text": "Physical Readout & Wavefunction Collapse",
          "role": "header",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            2.5,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_m0",
          "text": "Outcome 0: State collapses to |0\u27e9",
          "role": "body",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            0.5,
            0.1
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "txt_m1",
          "text": "Outcome 1: State collapses to |1\u27e9",
          "role": "body",
          "position": [
            0.0,
            -0.5,
            0.1
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visualElements": [
        {
          "id": "vis_7_bg",
